From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 release engines drop dangerous launch switches (ABI 1.56)

Security audit RC-500 F-03, second layer. Bridge 0.59.0, feature
launch_switch_filter. ReArcEngineRun passed every argv switch to ChromeMain,
so any process running as the user could relaunch ReArc on the real profile
with --remote-debugging-port and read every cookie over CDP (Chrome closes
that route only for Google Chrome branding). A release (NDEBUG) engine now
drops the --remote-debugging-* family, --remote-allow-origins, --no-sandbox,
--disable-gpu-sandbox, --disable-web-security, --disable-site-isolation-
trials, --js-flags, the *-cmd-prefix, launcher and subprocess-path switches,
--ignore-certificate-errors, --proxy-server, --proxy-pac-url, --unsafely-
treat-insecure-origin-as-secure, --allow-running-insecure-content and
--enable-automation, in --name and -name spellings. --load-extension,
--disable-extensions-except, --host-resolver-rules and --ignore-certificate-
errors-spki-list pass only after ReArcEngineAllowTestSwitches, which the shell
calls for its own self-test. Debug engines pass everything through for
engine/tests.

Last rebased: 2026-11-10 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.96 (2ad9b7f5a8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

